<pdd-reason>The PRD's core loop is 'an AI agent changed my mix, I press refresh and see what changed'; without an append-only record the What-changed strip has nothing to render.</pdd-reason>
<pdd-interface>
{
  "type": "module",
  "module": {
    "functions": [
      {
        "name": "append",
        "signature": "append(slug, actor, action, detail, rev_before, rev_after, author=None) -> None",
        "sideEffects": "single O_APPEND write to plans/<slug>/journal.jsonl",
        "errors": [
          "ValueError on unknown actor/author"
        ]
      },
      {
        "name": "read",
        "signature": "read(slug, limit=50, *, actor=None, author=None) -> list[dict]",
        "returns": "newest-first entries; truncated tail skipped"
      }
    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_types_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>
<pdd-dependency>brain/plan_paths_Python.prompt</pdd-dependency>

% Goal

Implement and maintain `brain/plan_journal.py` as the Append-only JSON Lines journal at plans/<slug>/journal.jsonl, one valid JSON value per line written with compact separators. append(slug, actor, action, detail, rev_before, rev_after, author=None) issues a single O_APPEND write with no read-modify-write, so concurrent ThreadingHTTPServer threads cannot interleave a partial record. actor is validated against plan_types.Actor and author independently against plan_types.Author (actor=cli with author=llm is legal and is the case the PRD cares about); an unknown value for either raises. read(slug, limit, actor=None, author=None) returns newest-first and TOLERATES a truncated final line by skipping it rather than raising, because a crash mid-append must not make the whole journal unreadable. Lines written before the author field existed read back as author=None: the journal is append-only and cannot be rewritten.

% Product contract

- Preserve the exact public interface declared in `<pdd-interface>`.
- Treat the reviewed architecture description in this prompt as normative behavior.
- Keep plan identity, immutable track identity, revision guards, and non-destructive storage semantics intact across GUI, CLI, and agent callers.
- Preserve compatible behavior outside this module's stated responsibility; do not redesign unrelated mixing or playback logic.
- Reject malformed, stale, ambiguous, or unsafe writes explicitly instead of silently losing plan data.
- Keep the implementation deterministic where the contract describes deterministic behavior.
- Target Python 3.13+ for Python modules and baseline browser JavaScript without a bundler for browser modules.
- Inspect the current implementation, its declared dependency modules, and the focused tests before changing code. This is a brownfield source prompt: working, tested behavior not contradicted here remains part of the contract.

% Architecture detail

Append-only JSON Lines journal at plans/<slug>/journal.jsonl, one valid JSON value per line written with compact separators. append(slug, actor, action, detail, rev_before, rev_after, author=None) issues a single O_APPEND write with no read-modify-write, so concurrent ThreadingHTTPServer threads cannot interleave a partial record. actor is validated against plan_types.Actor and author independently against plan_types.Author (actor=cli with author=llm is legal and is the case the PRD cares about); an unknown value for either raises. read(slug, limit, actor=None, author=None) returns newest-first and TOLERATES a truncated final line by skipping it rather than raising, because a crash mid-append must not make the whole journal unreadable. Lines written before the author field existed read back as author=None: the journal is append-only and cannot be rewritten.

% Output

- Primary output: `brain/plan_journal.py`.
- PDD context tags: backend, plan, provenance.
- Keep changes scoped to the primary output and the smallest necessary caller/test adaptations.

% Verification

- Run the focused tests that cover `brain/plan_journal.py` and every declared interface.
- Run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m unittest discover -s tests` before accepting a repository-wide sync.
- For Python modules, also run `UV_CACHE_DIR=/private/tmp/claw-dj-uv-cache uv run python -m py_compile brain/plan_journal.py`.
- Verify revision-conflict, missing-file, malformed-input, and legacy-compatibility paths relevant to this module.
- Do not require a model, GitHub, Mixxx playback, or network access for deterministic tests.

